{"number":1,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-A1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"In Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs make the sample stack DATA: add SampleLayer (materialId + thickness : Thickness; materialId stays a string until step 2 elevates it), PeriodGroup (cell : SampleLayer list, count : int), StackItem = SingleLayer of SampleLayer | Repeated of PeriodGroup, and SampleStructure (films : StackItem list, substrate : SampleLayer option, lower : material-id option where None = vacuum) with a pure expansion member mirroring RepeatBuilder.expand (OpticalConstructor.Ui/RepeatBuilder.fs:24). Replace Sample.materialId + Sample.thickness (ElementId.fs:45-49) with structure : SampleStructure, keeping substrate : SubstrateKind (ElementId.fs:35) as the geometry facet; re-seed all 11 samples in Library.seedEntries (ElementId.fs:189) structurally - the quarter-wave stack becomes Repeated 20x[glass quarter-wave; vacuum quarter-wave] plus one trailing glass layer, the EUV stack Repeated 100x[Mo; Si], langasite-on-silicon becomes films [langasite] with lower = silicon. Add the missing built-ins to MaterialLibrary.builtInEntries (MaterialLibrary.fs:79): euv-molybdenum / euv-silicon over OpticalProperties.euvMolybdenum / euvSilicon (OpticalProperties/Standard.fs:110-111) and active-crystal over OpticalProperties.planarCrystal with n11 2.315, n33 2.226, rho12 1.5e-6 (the constants currently at Propagation.fs:115-119). In Propagation.fs delete the sample.id string branching of sampleToSystem (Propagation.fs:139-141,157,172,180) and the propertiesOf glass-fallback map (Propagation.fs:104-111): add resolveSampleMaterials : MaterialLibrary -> Sample -> Result<ResolvedSample, MaterialError> resolving every referenced material to its OpticalPropertiesWithDisp (an unknown id is a typed Error, never a fallback), rebuild sampleToSystem as a total ResolvedSample -> WaveLength -> OpticalSystem over the expanded structure (no rotation yet - step 20 adds it), and re-point sampleMueller and the sweep builders at ResolvedSample; hosts resolve once per run and surface the error as a message.","acceptance":"After the change, every seeded sample's structurally-built OpticalSystem at a reference wavelength MUST equal the previously hand-built system (film count, substrate, tensors), and resolving a sample that names an unknown material MUST return a typed Error - with the solution building and existing tests green.","section":"Part A - Structural samples, ids and proxies (CRITICAL - land first)"}
{"number":2,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-A2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[1],"how_to":"Add MaterialId and SampleId as Guid-backed single-case DUs (a value member, a static create unit -> id minting Guid.NewGuid) in OpticalConstructor.Domain; re-type MaterialEntry.id (MaterialLibrary.fs:33), Sample.id (ElementId.fs:45), SampleLayer.materialId and SampleStructure.lower to the elevated ids. Seeds mint FIXED literal Guids (Guid.Parse of literal strings at seed construction) so tests and the grouping trees stay deterministic; LibraryEntry.entryId (ElementId.fs:100) returns the Guid string form so the Selector valueId binding seam is unchanged, and the seedTrees leaves reference the seeded samples programmatically instead of repeating literals. resolveMaterial (MaterialLibrary.fs:69) becomes a MaterialId lookup; relabel MaterialError.UnknownMaterialId (MaterialLibrary.fs:42-43) to carry reason : string. Update every construction/lookup site: the MaterialImport entry builders (OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs:80,109,144), StackEditor.layerMaterialDrop (OpticalConstructor.Ui/StackEditor.fs:195), and the TestWindows host id literals. No legacy string-id path, no fallback, no migration.","acceptance":"After the change, no domain record carries a raw string material/sample id (MaterialId / SampleId are the field types) and create-store-lookup round-trips by id MUST pass in OpticalConstructor.Tests."}
{"number":3,"anchor":"ADD_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-A3","id":"STORE_XDUO_0001","name":"MaterialProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Domain","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[2],"how_to":"In OpticalConstructor.Domain, beside MaterialLibrary, declare the mutating materials write-seam: DispersionFilter = AnyDispersion | OnlyDispersive | OnlyNonDispersive; MaterialQuery (text : string, category : MaterialCategory option, dispersion : DispersionFilter - MaterialCategory at MaterialLibrary.fs:21); extend MaterialError with DuplicateMaterialId, MaterialStillReferenced and InvalidMaterial, each carrying reason : string; and the [<ReferenceEquality>] record MaterialProxy with listMaterials : unit -> Result<MaterialEntry list, MaterialError>, searchMaterials : MaterialQuery -> Result<MaterialEntry list, MaterialError>, tryGetMaterial : MaterialId -> Result<MaterialEntry option, MaterialError>, addMaterial : MaterialEntry -> Result<unit, MaterialError>, updateMaterial : MaterialEntry -> Result<unit, MaterialError>, removeMaterial : MaterialId -> Result<unit, MaterialError>, following the LibraryProxy functional-proxy convention (ElementId.fs:178-184). Provide a mock (an inline stub record over a fixed entry list) plus a mock-driven test in OpticalConstructor.Tests exercising every field.","acceptance":"After the step, a mock-driven test MUST build a stub MaterialProxy and exercise all six functions through their exact signatures, and it passes."}
{"number":4,"anchor":"ADD_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-A4","id":"STORE_XDUO_0002","name":"SampleProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Domain","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[2],"how_to":"In OpticalConstructor.Domain, beside Library, declare the mutating samples write-seam with the same functional-proxy shape as step 3: SampleQuery (text : string, substrate : SubstrateKind option - SubstrateKind at ElementId.fs:35); SampleError = UnknownSampleId | DuplicateSampleId | InvalidSample, each carrying reason : string; and the [<ReferenceEquality>] record SampleProxy with listSamples : unit -> Result<Sample list, SampleError>, searchSamples : SampleQuery -> Result<Sample list, SampleError>, tryGetSample : SampleId -> Result<Sample option, SampleError>, addSample : Sample -> Result<unit, SampleError>, updateSample : Sample -> Result<unit, SampleError>, removeSample : SampleId -> Result<unit, SampleError>. Provide a mock (an inline stub record over a fixed sample list) plus a mock-driven test in OpticalConstructor.Tests exercising every field.","acceptance":"After the step, a mock-driven test MUST build a stub SampleProxy and exercise all six functions through their exact signatures, and it passes."}
{"number":5,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-A4","id":"STORE_XDUO_0002","name":"SampleProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[4],"how_to":"Implement SampleProxy.createInMemory : unit -> SampleProxy closing over a ref Map<SampleId, Sample> seeded from the samples in Library.seedEntries (ElementId.fs:189) - the elevated SampleId is the Map key directly. addSample rejects a duplicate id (DuplicateSampleId), updateSample rejects an unknown id (UnknownSampleId), searchSamples filters by case-insensitive name fragment and the SubstrateKind facet. Mutation stays inside the closure (the IO boundary); the functions are deterministic under test because every entry carries its own id. Unit tests in OpticalConstructor.Tests: add-then-list, update-then-get, remove-then-search round-trips with fixed Guids, plus the duplicate-add and unknown-update rejections.","acceptance":"After createInMemory lands, add-then-list, update-then-get and remove-then-search round-trips over the stateful in-memory SampleProxy MUST pass deterministically with fixed Guids and no IO."}
{"number":6,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-A3","id":"STORE_XDUO_0001","name":"MaterialProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[3,5],"how_to":"Implement MaterialProxy.createInMemory taking samplesReferencing : MaterialId -> Sample list and closing over a ref Map<MaterialId, MaterialEntry> seeded from MaterialLibrary.builtInEntries (MaterialLibrary.fs:79). searchMaterials reuses the pure byCategory / byNameContains filters (MaterialLibrary.fs:53,57) plus the DispersionFilter facet (an entry is dispersive when its epsWithDisp is the func case). removeMaterial returns Error MaterialStillReferenced with a reason naming the referencing samples whenever samplesReferencing returns any - it never cascades and never silently deletes; addMaterial hard-blocks a duplicate id (DuplicateMaterialId). At composition the referencing lookup is backed by the SampleProxy store (step 5). Unit tests: add/update/remove/search round-trips, the referenced-material hard block, and the duplicate-add rejection.","acceptance":"After createInMemory lands, removeMaterial on a material referenced by a seeded sample MUST return Error MaterialStillReferenced and leave the store unchanged, while removing an unreferenced material succeeds - with the round-trip and search-facet tests passing."}
{"number":7,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-B1","touches":["Berreman","BerremanTests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"In Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs add the generic serializable formula blocks: WaveLengthInterval (lower : WaveLength, upper : WaveLength - an interval is just an interval); DispersionTerm (lambda : double, coefficients : double array, power : int, multiplier : double) meaning multiplier * (sum over k of coefficients[k] * (x - lambda)^k) ^ power; DispersionFormula (terms : DispersionTerm list, wavelengthScale : double = metres per coefficient unit) with member evaluate : WaveLength -> double reducing the canonical wavelength to the coefficient unit and summing the terms; and ComplexDispersionTerm / ComplexDispersionFormula mirroring them over System.Numerics.Complex (used ONLY where a model is inherently complex). These are pure data + evaluation; the engine unions in this file are untouched. BerremanTests: evaluate a Cauchy-shaped Laurent polynomial and a Sellmeier-shaped inverse term against hand-computed values, using the existing tolerance helpers (BerremanTests/MatrixComparison.fs) - no new epsilon logic.","acceptance":"After the step, DispersionFormula.evaluate MUST reproduce hand-computed polynomial and inverse-polynomial values within the project tolerance in BerremanTests.","section":"Part B - Serializable dispersion values (engine)"}
{"number":8,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-B2","touches":["Berreman","BerremanTests"],"depends_on":[7],"how_to":"In Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs add the serializable eps tree: ConstantEpsValue - a DESCRIPTIVE DU, never a bare Eps - with the six cases IsotropicTransparent of RefractionIndex, IsotropicAbsorbing of ComplexRefractionIndex, UniaxialTransparent of ordinary * extraordinary RefractionIndex, UniaxialAbsorbing of ordinary * extraordinary ComplexRefractionIndex, BiaxialTransparent of nx * ny * nz RefractionIndex, BiaxialAbsorbing of nx * ny * nz ComplexRefractionIndex (index types at MaterialProperties.fs:35,43) and member toEps building through the existing constructors Eps.fromRefractionIndex / Eps.fromComplexRefractionIndex (MaterialProperties.fs:76,79,87,95; uniaxial maps to the triple n_o, n_e, n_o); EpsAxisDispersion = RealNK of n * k DispersionFormula (k = the zero formula for transparent media) | ComplexEps of ComplexDispersionFormula, with member complexIndex : WaveLength -> ComplexRefractionIndex (RealNK evaluates n + i*k; ComplexEps evaluates sqrt of eps); IsotropicEpsSegment / UniaxialEpsSegment / BiaxialEpsSegment, each one wavelengthInterval : WaveLengthInterval SHARED across that segment's axes plus one EpsAxisDispersion per axis; EpsDispersiveValue = IsotropicDispersive | UniaxialDispersive | BiaxialDispersive of the homogeneous segment lists; and EpsWithDispValue = EpsWithDispValue of EpsDispersiveValue | EpsWithoutDispValue of ConstantEpsValue with member toEpsWithDisp : EpsWithDisp - the constant case short-circuits to EpsWithoutDisp via toEps, the dispersive case builds the WaveLength -> Eps closure selecting the FIRST segment whose interval covers the wavelength (top-of-list wins on overlap; when none covers, the topmost segment extrapolates - no clamps, no validation). BerremanTests: every ConstantEpsValue case equals the directly-constructed Eps; segment selection (overlap -> first, out-of-range -> topmost); uniaxial and biaxial dispersive closures equal the per-axis analytic values.","acceptance":"After the step, EpsWithDispValue.toEpsWithDisp MUST reproduce the directly-constructed engine Eps for all six constant cases, and the top-of-list overlap and topmost-extrapolation segment tests MUST pass in BerremanTests."}
{"number":9,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-B3","touches":["Berreman","OpticalProperties","BerremanTests"],"depends_on":[7],"how_to":"In Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs add Handedness = LeftHanded | RightHanded (the enantiomorph is one overall sign flip of g); the NAMED generic gyration records UniaxialGyration (g11, g33), Orthorhombic222Gyration (g11, g22, g33), Monoclinic2Gyration (g11, g22, g33, g13), MonoclinicMGyration (g12, g23), Triclinic1Gyration (g11, g22, g33, g23, g13, g12) - never anonymous tuples; GyrationClass<'g> = CubicActive of 'g | UniaxialActive of UniaxialGyration | PlanarActive of 'g | Orthorhombic222 | Monoclinic2 | MonoclinicM | Triclinic1 over those records (ONLY rotation-producing classes; no free 3x3); GyrotropicValue<'g> (gyration : GyrationClass<'g>, hand : Handedness); and RhoWithDispValue = RhoWithDispValue of GyrotropicValue<DispersionFormula> | RhoWithoutDispValue of GyrotropicValue<RhoValue> (RhoValue at MaterialProperties.fs:127). Because the core project cannot reference OpticalProperties, implement toRhoWithDisp : RhoWithDisp as a type extension in Berreman/OpticalProperties/Active.fs, assembling the imaginary gyration matrix through the existing constructors - CubicActive via Rho.cubicCrystal (Active.fs:30), UniaxialActive via the diagonal Rho.type_3_4_6_Crystal (Active.fs:46; NOT type_32_42_62_Crystal, Active.fs:54, which needs a g12 a symmetric two-component uniaxial cannot supply), PlanarActive via Rho.planarCrystal (Active.fs:38) - and NEW Rho.fromIm builders added to Active.fs for 222, monoclinic-2, monoclinic-m and triclinic (Rho.fromIm at MaterialProperties.fs:139). The dispersive case evaluates each component's DispersionFormula at the wavelength; RhoWithoutDispValue short-circuits to RhoWithoutDisp. BerremanTests: the quartz class-32 example (g11 +5.9e-5, g33 -10.1e-5) assembles diag(g11, g11, g33); each new builder is covered; flipping Handedness negates the tensor.","acceptance":"After the step, each GyrationClass case MUST assemble the expected imaginary gyration matrix (quartz example diag(+5.9e-5, +5.9e-5, -10.1e-5) via Rho.type_3_4_6_Crystal; handedness flip negates it) and the new 222/monoclinic/triclinic builders MUST be covered by passing tests."}
{"number":10,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-B4","touches":["Berreman","BerremanTests"],"depends_on":[7],"how_to":"In Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs add GyrationAxis = AlongX | AlongY | AlongZ (default AlongZ, the Faraday geometry; transverse = Voigt); PolderValue<'g> (muDiagonal : 'g, muParallel : 'g, gyration : 'g, axis : GyrationAxis) - ONE generic Polder record reused by both cases; ConstantMuValue = ScalarMu of MuValue | GyromagneticMu of PolderValue<MuValue> (MuValue at MaterialProperties.fs:101); and MuWithDispValue = MuWithDispValue of PolderValue<DispersionFormula> | MuWithoutDispValue of ConstantMuValue with member toMuWithDisp : MuWithDisp assembling the Polder tensor rows [mu, +i*g, 0], [-i*g, mu, 0], [0, 0, muParallel] permuted by axis through Mu.create (MaterialProperties.fs:112); ScalarMu builds mu times identity; the constant cases short-circuit to MuWithoutDisp. No solver work - the Berreman matrix already reads off-diagonal mu. BerremanTests: each axis produces the correctly permuted tensor; ScalarMu equals the scaled identity; a dispersive Polder value evaluated at a wavelength equals the constant assembly with the same magnitudes.","acceptance":"After the step, MuWithDispValue.toMuWithDisp MUST produce the expected Polder tensor for all three axes and the scalar short-circuit, verified in BerremanTests."}
{"number":11,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-B5","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[8],"how_to":"In OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs add a SumOfTerms escape-hatch case to DispersionModel (DispersionModels.fs:120) carrying a raw EpsAxisDispersion, and toEpsAxis : DispersionModel -> EpsAxisDispersion lowering each analytic case: Cauchy (coefficients at :51) to RealNK Laurent terms (A + B*x^-2 + C*x^-4, k = the zero formula); Sellmeier (:42) to RealNK using the identity that each oscillator is a constant B_i plus an inverse term with the n formula evaluating sqrt(1 + sum); ConstantNK (:109) to RealNK constants; Lorentz (:63) and Drude (:74) to ComplexEps inverse terms (complex is genuine - the damping); TaucLorentz (:85) and GaussianOscillator (:97) to ComplexEps wrapping evaluate (:206) as named transcendental cases (they are not finite term sums). Remove AnisotropicModel (:242) as superseded by EpsDispersiveValue, and re-point the toOpticalProperties (:228) / toAnisotropicOpticalProperties (:259) surface at EpsWithDispValue.toEpsWithDisp, keeping isotropicProperties (:216) as the single vacuum-mu/rho wrapper; update the existing consumers in OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs:62,70. Tests: for each analytic case, toEpsAxis complexIndex equals evaluate across a sampled wavelength grid within tolerance.","acceptance":"After the step, for Sellmeier, Cauchy, ConstantNK, Lorentz and Drude the lowered EpsAxisDispersion.complexIndex MUST match DispersionModels.evaluate across a sampled wavelength grid within tolerance, and AnisotropicModel MUST no longer exist."}
{"number":12,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-B6","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[11],"how_to":"Add ForouhiBloomer and BrendelBormann cases to DispersionModel following the existing coefficient-record convention (coefficients + wavelengthUnit + thermoOptic option, as the records at DispersionModels.fs:42-115): Forouhi-Bloomer's amorphous n(E)/k(E) five-parameter form and Brendel-Bormann's Gaussian-broadened (Voigt) oscillator epsilon(E). Implement their evaluation in the same private baseIndex dispatch the other models use (:156) and lower both via toEpsAxis as ComplexEps wrapping evaluate. Tests reproduce documented reference values for one published coefficient set each (Forouhi-Bloomer 1986; Rakic et al. 1998 Au - references in the steering .spec-md) within tolerance.","acceptance":"After the step, evaluate for ForouhiBloomer and BrendelBormann MUST reproduce documented reference values for a published coefficient set within tolerance in OpticalConstructor.Tests."}
{"number":13,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-B7","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[8,9,10,11],"how_to":"In OpticalConstructor.Domain add the edit-model option tree MaterialComplexity (eps : EpsWithDispValue - ALWAYS present; magnetic : MuWithDispValue option; active : RhoWithDispValue option) with pure member toProperties : OpticalPropertiesWithDisp (Dispersion.fs:53) = eps.toEpsWithDisp plus Mu.vacuum.dispersive / Rho.vacuum.dispersive defaults for absent options. Add complexity : MaterialComplexity option to MaterialEntry (MaterialLibrary.fs:31): Some is the editable source of truth (properties = complexity.toProperties, kept in sync at save); None marks an engine-preset entry (view-only). Re-express the expressible built-ins as complexities - the four glasses as IsotropicTransparent, uniaxial/biaxial crystals as UniaxialTransparent/BiaxialTransparent, euv-molybdenum/euv-silicon as IsotropicAbsorbing, active-crystal as UniaxialTransparent plus a constant PlanarActive gyration - while silicon and langasite keep None (their dispersion is coded in OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs:98-99). Tests: toProperties supplies the vacuum mu/rho defaults when the options are None; each re-expressed built-in's toProperties matches the original preset's tensors at reference wavelengths.","acceptance":"After the step, every re-expressed built-in's complexity.toProperties MUST reproduce the original preset's OpticalProperties at reference wavelengths within tolerance, and toProperties MUST default absent magnetic/active options to vacuum."}
{"number":14,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-C1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"In OpticalConstructor.TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs rename the element-binding bay: BayNames.library (TableAndElementRotationView.fs:150, value 'Library') becomes BayNames.selector with value 'Selector'; update BayNames.all (:156) and the mainBays row (:1582) plus any test references. The bay's behaviour - kind-constrained, confirm-gated binding through LibraryControls and the read-only LibraryProxy - is unchanged; LibraryControls and LibraryProxy keep their names (only the label frees the word Library for the samples workbench).","acceptance":"After the rename, the ribbon MUST show a Selector tab with the unchanged confirm-gated binding behaviour and no bay labelled Library, verified by the headless UI tests.","section":"Part C - Bays: Selector, Materials, Library"}
{"number":15,"anchor":"ADD_COMPONENT","ac":"AC-C2","id":"UICOMP_XDUO_0001","name":"MaterialsControls","kind":"component","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Controls","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"Create OpticalConstructor.Controls/MaterialsControls.fs copying the domain-free LibraryControls shape (LibraryControls.fs:25,34,64,76: pure Row and State records, a Handlers record of unit-returning functions, one [<RequireQualifiedAccess>] module UiIds of [<Literal>] ids): a searchable materials list with a search box, category and dispersion facet selectors, and Add / Edit / Remove / View verbs. Stable intent-named ids: MaterialSearchBox, MaterialCategoryFilter, MaterialDispersionFilter, MaterialsList, AddMaterialButton, EditMaterialButton, RemoveMaterialButton, ViewMaterialButton. The control renders the rows it is given and never touches a proxy (the host flattens); rows for view-only entries (no edit model) carry no Edit affordance - removed, not greyed. Headless structure test in OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests: mount the view over a known State, assert every UiIds control exists, and assert a simulated click dispatches the matching handler.","acceptance":"After the step, the headless test MUST mount MaterialsControls over a known State, find every UiIds control, and observe that a simulated Add click invokes the add handler."}
{"number":16,"anchor":"ADD_COMPONENT","ac":"AC-C3","id":"UICOMP_XDUO_0002","name":"SampleLibraryControls","kind":"component","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Controls","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"Create OpticalConstructor.Controls/SampleLibraryControls.fs with the same domain-free shape as step 15 (LibraryControls.fs:25,34,64,76 conventions) for the samples workbench: a searchable samples list with a search box and a substrate-kind facet selector, and Add / Edit / Remove / View verbs plus the multilayer entry point. Stable intent-named ids: SampleSearchBox, SampleSubstrateFilter, SamplesList, AddSampleButton, EditSampleButton, RemoveSampleButton, ViewSampleButton, MakeMultilayerButton. Headless structure test in OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests mirroring step 15.","acceptance":"After the step, the headless test MUST mount SampleLibraryControls over a known State, find every UiIds control, and observe that a simulated Add click invokes the add handler."}
{"number":17,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-D1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"REAL-MOVE the renderer-neutral chart model OpticalConstructor.TestWindows/ExperimentChart.fs (ExperimentChart :18, toCsv :47, ChartFontState :90, ChartElement :152, AxisStyle :199, SeriesStyle :229, ChartStyleState :241, dataBounds :261, defaultState :281) and the ScottPlot seam OpticalConstructor.TestWindows/ChartWindow.fs (rebuildPlot :178) into OpticalConstructor.Controls, changing their namespace and adding a ScottPlot.Avalonia 5.1.59 PackageReference to OpticalConstructor.Controls.fsproj (the same version both hosts already use: TestWindows fsproj:75, Ui fsproj:173). File-linking is NOT acceptable - it mints distinct type identities per assembly; this MUST be a real move plus project references. Re-point every TestWindows usage; reconcile OpticalConstructor.Ui/Charts/ChartSettings.fs onto the one shared model (re-point Ui, do not grow a third settings type). Both existing charts stay green.","acceptance":"After the move, the chart model and window types MUST compile in OpticalConstructor.Controls with both hosts re-pointed, existing chart tests green, and no chart type left declared in TestWindows.","section":"Part D - Shared chart and dual-axis n/k view"}
{"number":18,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-D2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[17],"how_to":"In the moved chart model add the second Y axis: ChartElement (formerly ExperimentChart.fs:152) distinguishes the left and right Y axes; ChartStyleState (:241) holds a second AxisStyle for the right axis with tri-state axis mutators (X, Y-left, Y-right); SeriesStyle (:229) gains an axis-side assignment (a two-case DU, left or right); dataBounds (:261) and defaultState (:281) compute independent per-axis Y bounds. In the moved ChartWindow, rebuildPlot (formerly ChartWindow.fs:178) assigns each scatter's Axes.YAxis to plot.Axes.Left or plot.Axes.Right (ScottPlot 5.1.59 native right axis, currently unused in the repo), and applyAxisLimits (:133), the axis format and font appliers, and setCartesianAxesVisible (:151) also drive plot.Axes.Right. The polar toggle stays hidden for non-angular charts (ExperimentChart.angular, :29); toCsv (:47) is unchanged. Model-level tests cover per-axis bounds and the left/right series assignment.","acceptance":"After the step, a chart carrying one left-axis and one right-axis series MUST produce independent per-axis Y bounds in dataBounds/defaultState and assign each scatter to its side in rebuildPlot, with toCsv output unchanged."}
{"number":19,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-D3","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[17,18],"how_to":"REAL-MOVE the pure spectral-axis helpers axisLabel / spectralRange / axisTicks (OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialPreview.fs:18,31,40) into an OpticalConstructor.Domain module and re-point MaterialPreview (no duplication). Add an Analytics ProjectReference to OpticalConstructor.TestWindows.fsproj (today it references only Domain and Controls, fsproj:79,81) and build a pure nkDispersionChart builder in TestWindows: OpticalPropertiesWithDisp + display unit + range -> the shared ExperimentChart, with the n series (Analytics.Variables.calculateN11Re, Analytics/Variables.fs:321 - the builder behind plotN11Series, OpticalConstructor.Ui/Charts/SeriesData.fs:103) assigned to the LEFT axis and the k series (calculateXi11Im, behind plotXi11Series, SeriesData.fs:104) to the RIGHT, X axis from the moved spectral-axis helpers. Dispersive entries yield curves; non-dispersive entries yield flat lines through the same builder.","acceptance":"After the step, nkDispersionChart over a dispersive entry MUST yield an ExperimentChart whose n series is assigned to the left axis and k series to the right, spanning the requested spectral range - verified by a headless model test."}
{"number":20,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-E1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[1,2],"how_to":"In OpticalConstructor.Domain add CrystalOrientation = PrimaryAxes | EulerRotation of convention : RotationConvention * phi : Angle * theta : Angle * psi : Angle (RotationConvention at Geometry.fs:578, Rotation at :601) with member toRotation : Rotation - PrimaryAxes is the identity, EulerRotation builds Rotation.create convention phi theta psi (Geometry.fs:604); the named shortcuts rotatePiX / rotateHalfPiY (:616,622) remain available for tests. Give SampleLayer an orientation : CrystalOrientation field defaulting to PrimaryAxes, and apply it in the step-1 system builder via Layer.rotate (Media.fs:30) -> OpticalProperties.rotate (MaterialProperties.fs:187) for non-identity orientations - nothing is stored rotated (worked precedent: Analytics/Examples/ActiveCrystalComparison.fsx:136 rotates a plate system by rotateHalfPiY). Tests in OpticalConstructor.Tests: an EulerRotation layer's built system equals rotating the same layer directly; PrimaryAxes builds unrotated tensors.","acceptance":"After the step, a uniaxial layer with an EulerRotation orientation MUST produce the same rotated tensors as applying Layer.rotate directly, and PrimaryAxes MUST leave tensors unrotated - verified in OpticalConstructor.Tests.","section":"Part E - Sample editing: orientation, period groups, bulk ops"}
{"number":21,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-E2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[20],"how_to":"Add a pure, Avalonia-free Domain edit model SampleStackEditor over SampleStructure, mirroring the message-DU discipline of StackEditor.StackMsg / applyStackMsg (OpticalConstructor.Ui/StackEditor.fs:161,176) but at the material-id level: a state record (structure : SampleStructure, selection : selected layer positions) and messages SelectLayer, SelectByMaterial of MaterialId, ClearSelection, SetThicknessOfSelected of Thickness, SetMaterialOfSelected of MaterialId, SetOrientationOfSelected of CrystalOrientation, RemoveSelected, MoveSelectedUp, MoveSelectedDown, MakeRepeatBlock of count : int (folds the selected contiguous layers into a PeriodGroup), SetRepeatCount of group position * int - rejecting count < 1 with a typed error (the same rule Validation.validateRepeatCount enforces at the Ui boundary, OpticalConstructor.Ui/Validation.fs:56). Editing a period's cell edits every repetition; changing the count adds or removes whole periods. This is DISTINCT from the untouched StackEditor.groupLayers (StackEditor.fs:69) - the existing OpticalSystem editor stays as-is. Every message arm is unit-tested without a window.","acceptance":"After the step, MakeRepeatBlock over 2 selected layers with count K MUST yield a structure expanding to 2*K films, and SelectByMaterial followed by SetThicknessOfSelected MUST update exactly the matching layers - verified by pure unit tests."}
{"number":22,"anchor":"ADD_COMPONENT","ac":"AC-E3","id":"UICOMP_XDUO_0003","name":"SampleEditorWindow","kind":"component","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","touches":["OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[5,6,16,20,21],"how_to":"Create the Sample editor window in OpticalConstructor.TestWindows beside the existing pop-out ChartWindow.fs: name and description fields, the SubstrateKind geometry facet, and the stack table over the step-21 SampleStackEditor - each PeriodGroup renders as one collapsible super-row (rotating-triangle expander) with an inline repeat-count stepper and its unit-cell layers nested beneath; multi-select plus a bulk toolbar (select-by-material, set thickness, change material, set orientation, remove, move up/down, make repeat block) dispatching SampleStackEditor messages; material choice by MaterialId from MaterialProxy.listMaterials; the per-layer orientation editor is shown ONLY for anisotropic materials (removed for isotropic, not greyed); optional QWOT entry derives the physical thickness t = lambda/(4n) read-only into canonical metres (precedent: the DBR template expansion Templates.dbrCell / Templates.dbrPeriods, OpticalConstructor.Ui/Templates.fs:103,106). Save calls SampleProxy.addSample for a new sample (minting SampleId.create) and updateSample for an existing one; Cancel discards; Save/Cancel sit in one row with distinct positive/negative styling. Stable UiIds: SampleEditorWindow, SampleNameBox, AddLayerButton, MakeRepeatBlockButton, SelectByMaterialButton, SetLayerHeightButton, SetLayerMaterialButton, SetOrientationOfSelectedButton, RemoveSelectedLayersButton, RepeatCountStepper, QwotEntryBox, SampleEditorSaveButton, SampleEditorCancelButton.","acceptance":"After the step, headless tests MUST drive the window by UiIds: repeating a 2-layer selection K times shows a structure expanding to 2*K films, select-by-material bulk set-thickness updates only matching layers, and Save persists through SampleProxy (add for new, update for existing)."}
{"number":23,"anchor":"ADD_COMPONENT","ac":"AC-F1","id":"UICOMP_XDUO_0004","name":"MaterialEditorWindow","kind":"component","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","touches":["OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[6,13,19],"how_to":"Create the Material editor window in OpticalConstructor.TestWindows over a pure MaterialComplexity edit model (an Avalonia-free message DU plus update function in OpticalConstructor.Domain, unit-tested without a window). Progressive-unlock ladder: the anisotropy 3-way choice (isotropic / uniaxial / biaxial selecting the ConstantEpsValue shape or EpsDispersiveValue flavor), the absorbing toggle (transparent vs absorbing constant cases), the dispersive toggle (ConstantEpsValue vs segment list), and the OPTIONAL optically-active and magnetic toggles - each unlock lifts exactly one aspect off its default and unchecking restores that default losslessly. Per-segment dispersion editor: wavelengthInterval bounds plus a DispersionModel picker including ForouhiBloomer, BrendelBormann and the raw SumOfTerms escape hatch, lowered via toEpsAxis. Symmetry-class gyration panel constrained by the anisotropy choice (isotropic offers cubic 23/432; uniaxial offers the diagonal two-component classes; biaxial offers 222/monoclinic/triclinic; a handedness switch; the activity toggle is REMOVED for non-rotating choices, not greyed). Polder-mu panel: scalar or gyromagnetic with the axis picker. The live preview embeds the step-19 dual-axis n/k chart; a negative k surfaces the advisory gain warning (the imaginaryIndexGainWarning rule, OpticalConstructor.Ui/Validation.fs:92). Save mints MaterialId.create for a new entry and calls MaterialProxy.addMaterial / updateMaterial, storing complexity = Some model with properties = toProperties; entries with complexity = None (silicon, langasite) are view-only and offer no Edit affordance. Stable UiIds: MaterialEditorWindow, MaterialNameBox, AnisotropyToggle, AbsorbingToggle, DispersiveToggle, ActiveToggle, MagneticToggle, GyrationClassPicker, HandednessSwitch, DispersionModelPicker, AddSegmentButton, MaterialEditorSaveButton, MaterialEditorCancelButton.","acceptance":"After the step, headless tests MUST show: choosing biaxial exposes three principal-index fields, enabling activity on a uniaxial medium offers only the uniaxial gyration classes, unchecking a toggle restores the default model losslessly, and Save round-trips the entry through MaterialProxy with complexity = Some.","section":"Part F - Material editor"}
{"number":24,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-C4","touches":["OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[5,6,14,15,16,19,22,23],"how_to":"In TableAndElementRotationView add BayNames.materials with value 'Materials' and BayNames.library with value 'Library' (the samples workbench - the label freed by the step-14 Selector rename) to the BayNames module (:144-156) and mainBays (:1577); thread MaterialProxy and SampleProxy into the host model through initMainWith, updating the composition call mechanically so the solution builds (OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs:125-127; the final WIRE_UI step owns the composition acceptance). Flatten listMaterials/searchMaterials and listSamples/searchSamples results into MaterialsControls / SampleLibraryControls rows and map their Handlers to Msgs exactly as libraryState / flattenNode do for the Selector (TableAndElementRotationView.fs:1012,999). Verbs: the search boxes and facet selectors drive proxy queries; View shows read-only metadata plus the step-19 dual-axis n/k chart for materials and the LayerBandsControls band view over the expanded stack for samples (as the Details bay already renders); Add/Edit open the step-22/23 editor windows; Remove is confirm-gated inline, and a MaterialStillReferenced block surfaces as an inline message naming the referencing samples - never a cascade. Every verb re-queries its proxy so the list refreshes in the same render pass.","acceptance":"After the step, headless tests MUST drive both bays end to end by UiIds: search filters the rows, Add/Edit open the editor windows, removing a referenced material surfaces the MaterialStillReferenced message and leaves the store unchanged, and removing an unreferenced entry updates the list in the same render pass.","section":"Part C - Bays live (host wiring)"}
{"number":25,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-G1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[11],"how_to":"Extend MaterialImport.importRefractiveIndexInfo (OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs:109) beyond tabulated + formula 1: parse RII formulas 2 (Sellmeier-2), 3 (polynomial), 4 (the RII formula), 5 (Cauchy), 6 (gases) and 7 (Herzberger), each lowered through a DispersionModel or SumOfTerms to an EpsAxisDispersion carried in an EpsWithDispValue-backed MaterialComplexity on the imported MaterialEntry (so imports are editable); formulas 8 and 9 return a NEW typed unsupported-formula case on ImportError (MaterialImport.fs:29). Wavelengths keep the micrometre RII convention through the existing Units seam exactly as the formula 1 path already does. Tests in OpticalConstructor.Tests: one fixture per supported formula number asserting the imported entry's evaluated index matches hand-computed values at sample wavelengths; one fixture asserting formulas 8 and 9 produce the typed error.","acceptance":"After the step, importing fixtures for RII formulas 2-7 MUST produce entries whose evaluated index matches hand-computed values within tolerance, and formulas 8/9 MUST return the typed unsupported-formula ImportError.","section":"Part G - RII import breadth"}
{"number":26,"anchor":"WIRE_UI","ac":"AC-W1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[24,25],"how_to":"Finalize the composition root: MainConstructorWindow (OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs:114-129) builds MaterialProxy.createInMemory (its samplesReferencing lookup backed by the SampleProxy store) and SampleProxy.createInMemory beside the existing library/experiments proxies (Program.fs:125-126) and injects all four through initMainWith; the launcher path is otherwise unchanged. Verify the whole surface headless: the ui-smoke suite renders one frame for the Selector, Materials and Library bays and both editor windows without throwing.","acceptance":"After composition, launching the Main window MUST wire the four in-memory proxies at the root, and the ui-smoke suite MUST render the Selector, Materials and Library bays and both editor windows without throwing, with every test gate at or above its baseline count.","section":"Composition root"}
